{"type":"message-part","messageId":"b37e7301-fb68-45dd-be52-7054bcb3f3b2","role":"user","index":1,"part":{"type":"text","text":"# Managing Multiple Slack Accounts with Composio\n\n## Background\n\nComposio allows users to connect multiple accounts for the same toolkit (e.g., personal and work Slack). You can use aliases to distinguish between these accounts and programmatically select which one to use for a specific action.\n\n## Requirements\n\n1. Create a Python script `multi_slack.py` in `/home/user/multi-account-task`.\n2. Use the Composio Python SDK and the OpenAI SDK.\n3. Create a Composio session for the user `zealt-user01` with `multi_account` mode enabled.\n4. The script must connect two Slack accounts for this user, assigning them the aliases `work-slack` and `personal-slack`.\n5. For the purpose of this task, you can assume the accounts are already connected or simulate the connection flow by generating the auth links.\n6. The script must then send a message \"Hello from Work!\" to the `#general` channel using the `work-slack` account.\n7. The script must send a message \"Hello from Personal!\" to the `#general` channel using the `personal-slack` account.\n8. Both messages must be sent via an AI agent that is instructed to use the correct account based on the alias.\n\n## Implementation Guide\n\n1. Initialize `Composio` with `OpenAIProvider`.\n2. Create a session for `zealt-user01` with `multi_account={'enable': True}`.\n3. Use `session.authorize('slack', alias='work-slack')` and `session.authorize('slack', alias='personal-slack')` to ensure both connections exist.\n4. Initialize an OpenAI agent with the session tools.\n5. Prompt the agent to: \"Send 'Hello from Work!' to #general using the 'work-slack' account, and 'Hello from Personal!' to #general using the 'personal-slack' account.\"\n\n## Constraints\n\n* Project path: /home/user/multi-account-task\n* Use the test user `zealt-user01`.\n* Use the aliases `work-slack` and `personal-slack`.\n\n## Integrations\n\n* Composio\n* Slack\n* OpenAI"}}
